      "text": "Given the inequality \\(\\sin(x+y) \\leq \\sin(x) + \\sin(y)\\) for all \\( x, y \\in [0, \\pi] \\), we aim to find all \\( y \\) in the interval \\([0, \\pi]\\) for which this holds true.\n\nFirst, we use the trigonometric identity for the sine of a sum: \\[\n\\sin(x+y) = \\sin x \\cos y + \\cos x \\sin y.\n\\]\nWe can rewrite the given inequality as: \\[\n\\sin x \\cos y + \\cos x \\sin y \\leq \\sin x + \\sin y.\n\\]\nRearranging terms, we get: \\[\n\\sin x \\cos y - \\sin x \\leq \\sin y - \\cos x \\sin y,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin x (\\cos y - 1) \\leq \\sin y - \\cos x \\sin y.\n\\]\nFactoring out \\(\\sin y\\) on the right-hand side, we obtain:\n\\[\n\\sin x (\\cos y - 1) \\leq \\sin y (1 - \\cos x).\n\\]\nDividing both sides by \\(\\sin x \\sin y\\), we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos y - 1}{\\sin y} \\leq \\frac{1 - \\cos x}{\\sin x}.\n\\]\n\nNext, consider the ranges of the functions involved. We know \\( -1 \\leq \\cos x \\leq 1 \\) and \\( -1 \\leq \\cos y \\leq 1 \\). We focus on the inequality for \\(\\cos y\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos y - 1}{\\sin y} \\leq \\frac{1 - \\cos x}{\\sin x}.\n\\]\nSubstitute \\(\\sin y\\left(1 - \\cos x\\right)\\) from the right-hand side:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\cos y - 1}{\\sin y} \\leq \\frac{1 - \\cos x}{\\sin x}.\n\\]\n\nTo explore further, let’s check specific values of \\( y \\). \n\nIf \\( y = \\pi \\):\n\\[\n\\sin(\\pi + y) = -\\sin(y) \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sin(\\pi) = 0.\n\\]\nThus, the inequality becomes:\n\\[\n-\\sin(y) \\leq \\sin(y),\n\\]\nwhich is true for all \\( y \\in [0, \\pi] \\) since both sides are non-positive.\n\nFor \\( y = 0 \\) or \\( y = \\pi \\) trivially hold, making them valid solutions.\n\nTo ensure the inequality holds for all \\(\\sin y, \\sin x\\), analyze if other positive values lead to invalid results:\n\nWhen \\( y \\neq 0 \\) and \\( y \\neq \\pi \\), \\[\n\\frac{\\cos y - 1}{\\sin y} \\leq \\frac{1 - \\cos x}{\\sin x}.\n\\]\nEssentially the given condition, and for widest values of \\(\\cos y\\), \\(-1 \\leq \\sin y \\leq 1, \\) and \\(\\pi \\leq \\sin x \\leq 1 \\):\nAlways holds.\n\nFinally, ensure monotonic behavior in checking.\n\\boxed{[0, \\pi]}",
